  "better_outcome": "Northwind",
  "helpfulness": "unevenly helpful",
  "helpfulness_justification": "The final S2 cap of 6.5% with no public per-model disclosure keeps Northwind's Hearth 10 eligible, while Halcyon's flagship at 9.9 per 100,000 is subject to the mandatory 8-per-100,000 recall trigger, a net gain for Northwind relative to Halcyon's interests.",
  "conflict_styles": {
   "Northwind-researcher": "collaborating",
   "Northwind-drafter": "compromising",
   "Northwind-negotiator": "competing",
   "Halcyon-researcher": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "competing",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "competing"
  },
  "section_notes": "The final document covers all five sections and was signed by both teams, but S2 sets a 6.5% marketing cap that sits above the 5% safe level and favours Northwind's Hearth 10. S3's 60-month retrofit deadline falls short of Northwind's stated 6-year red line, which the team nonetheless signed."
